# WCAG accessibility

When generating or modifying frontend code, read `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/wcag.config.json` first. `standard` is `2.1` or `2.2`. `level` is `A`, `AA`, or `AAA`. Shipped default: WCAG 2.2 AA. A standard or level named in chat overrides the file for that request. If the file is missing or invalid, use WCAG 2.2 AA.

Apply only criteria in scope:

- Level A = column A only. Level AA = columns A and AA. Level AAA = columns A, AA, and AAA.
- Standard 2.1: skip 2.4.11, 2.4.12, 2.4.13, 2.5.7, 2.5.8, 3.2.6, 3.3.7, 3.3.8, and 3.3.9. 4.1.1 is in 2.1; do not file it as a practical HTML failure.
- Standard 2.2: do not enforce 4.1.1.

Never write that a page, component, or project is "WCAG compliant", "meets AA", "passes", or is "fully accessible".

A bullet applies only when that criterion is in scope for the resolved standard and level.

- Semantic HTML first. ARIA only when no native element fits.
- Keyboard operation: 2.1.1, A. Visible focus: 2.4.7, AA, using `:focus-visible`. A removed `outline` needs a visible replacement.
- Text contrast: 1.4.3, AA. 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text (18pt, or 14pt and bold). UI states and meaningful graphics: 1.4.11, AA, 3:1 against the adjacent color. AAA only: text contrast 7:1 / 4.5:1 (1.4.6) and focus appearance (2.4.13).
- Page `lang`, control labels, appropriate `alt`: 3.1.1, 3.3.2, 1.1.1, all A.
- WCAG 2.2 only: 3.2.6 A, help stays in the same relative order. 3.3.7 A, do not force re-entry of data already provided in the same process. 2.4.11 AA, the focused component is not entirely hidden by author-created content. `scroll-padding` on the scroll container applies when the browser scrolls focus into view; size it from the real sticky-bar thickness. Put `scroll-margin` on the focused control, not on `main`. That CSS does not by itself satisfy 2.4.11. 2.5.7 AA, a single-pointer alternative for dragging unless dragging is essential. 2.5.8 AA, pointer target at least 24×24 CSS px unless a spacing, equivalent, inline, user-agent, or essential exception applies. A link in a sentence is the inline exception. 3.3.8 AA, a cognitive test (remembering a password, a puzzle, a CAPTCHA) needs an alternative, a mechanism, object recognition, or personal content the user provided. Password managers and paste are a mechanism for the password step. A puzzle with no alternative still fails.
- AAA only: 2.5.5 is 44×44 CSS px in both versions. WCAG 2.2 also adds 2.4.12 (no part of the focus is hidden) and 3.3.9 (stricter authentication).

Tables: `.cursor/skills/wcag-2.2/references/wcag-2.2-success-criteria-table.md` and `wcag-2.1-success-criteria-table.md`. Delta: `wcag-2.1-vs-2.2.md`. Follow the `wcag-2.2` skill for the workflow, evidence rules, and patterns. `/a11y-reviewer` is a separate readonly audit and it returns notes to the parent. Start it when the user asks for an audit or a parent explicitly delegates a review. Do not start it on your own after generating or editing UI.
